# kernel-leanfix.config — match multi_v7's boot-critical settings that vendor's
# alientek_rk3506_defconfig differs on. The lean (vendor) config loaded + started
# but data-aborted at kernel entry (0x0208031c). Two diffs vs the proven-booting
# multi_v7; align both:
#   1. ARM_ATAG_DTB_COMPAT — multi_v7 has it, vendor lacks it. The RK boot chain
#      (vendor SPL/OP-TEE) likely hands ATAGs to the kernel; without this the
#      kernel can't fold them into the DTB and faults early.
#   2. VMSPLIT — vendor uses 3G_OPT (PAGE_OFFSET 0xB0000000); multi_v7 uses 3G
#      (0xC0000000). Match the standard.
CONFIG_ARM_ATAG_DTB_COMPAT=y
CONFIG_ARM_ATAG_DTB_COMPAT_CMDLINE_EXTEND=y
CONFIG_VMSPLIT_3G=y
# CONFIG_VMSPLIT_3G_OPT is not set
